# The mathkernel subsystem is stored BYTE-EXACT: frozen artifacts are pinned by sha256 and must not be
# altered by end-of-line normalization or textual patch round-trips. The CSV evidence is CRLF as frozen
# (its sha256 is of those exact bytes), so the CSVs are marked `binary` -- git format-patch then emits a
# literal-byte patch and git am writes the exact bytes (a textual diff would strip the CR). Other files
# are LF and kept un-normalized.
* -text
*.csv binary
